Not having very many altars in a given game is already rough.  It seems
like capping the number of artifacts based on the number of altars would
only serve to worsen this.  It makes altar generation far too important.
I'm already advantaged enough in a game with 8 altars, and disadvantaged
enough in a game with just 1.

Perhaps something almost inverse of this would make more sense -- the more
altars you have, the less likely it is to get an artifact.  I have no
logical (storyline) reason for this, but I like it for game balance.  In
those games that are just loaded with altars, so you can get holy water
and intrinsics and spellbooks and AC at will, you're less likely to get
artifacts; in games where you only have one altar, you can at least come
away with a decent number of artifacts.

You might even make it so that it depends on the number of co-aligned
altars in the game -- meaning you might not want to try to convert every
altar.  This would create an interesting choice sometimes.  And, of
course, if altar generation also depended on artifact generation... well,
then you really have a choice to make.



